{
  "_note": "The blast-radius trigger map for tools/gate_select.py (issue #294, HQ ruling n=2106). `gates` maps a gate (as tools/audit.py registers it) to the path globs whose change REQUIRES that gate; `floor` gates run on every commit; `default` is `full`. DEFAULT-DENY is the safety property, and it is NOT the map's completeness: any changed path matching no declared glob forces the FULL gate set, so an incomplete map degrades to slow and never to silent. Globs use fnmatch semantics where `*` also crosses `/`, so over-inclusion is deliberate -- a gate listed on a path it does not read only costs time, while a gate MISSING from a path it reads is the silent miss this map exists to remove. The map is DECLARED, never the change author's hand-pick; the gate set is derived from the changed paths alone. Authored conservatively: when a gate's read set was uncertain, its globs were widened. Regenerate the shape only by editing this file's own content, never by hand-picking at commit time.",
